A||||9||hugh||3rd brake light in spoiler||||5||
Z||000000||hugh||04-03-2001||07:11 PM||||I want to install a 3rd brake light in my spoiler because my rear scoop hides the original one in the car.Has anyone done this?I was also thinking of mounting one in/on the scoop instead of the spoiler.Any ideas?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/hugh_sig.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||04-03-2001||07:30 PM||||It's no big deal to wire... just tap the OE one's wires and run them into the deck lid using the power lock & ajar switch passage.<P>I don't know what you can use for a light. Keep in mind there are legal requirments that light has to meet to pass inspection. You want it to look like it belongs there or NJ inspection may fail you. For that reason you should probably leave the OE light connected even after the wing is wired. Those inspectors can get pretty flaky about things whien they feel like it.<P>Most of the premade LED bars I've seen are expensive. Dig around some of the elecronics suppliers. I can't remember who I saw that had them. One source might be to try parts yards for a wrecked wing or decklid you might could dig one out of.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Taijiguy||04-03-2001||07:48 PM||||I've thought about the LED thing, and am actually planning on employing them in my current "top secret" project. They're easy to make, the LED's are dirt cheap (like 5 for a buck or something at Radio Shack, and the parts to drop the voltage are equally as cheap. (basically just a couple of resistors) The most difficult part would be forming the light into the wing. Be sure to post pics if you pull this one off!<BR>~Taiji||||reg||1
Z||000003||Philphine||04-03-2001||08:12 PM||||i saw one molded/cut into an indy scoop. i want to try that. i've seen some long thin ones in the custom truck mags. just keeping an eye out for something i can use.||||reg||1
Z||000004||hugh||04-03-2001||08:17 PM||||I was hoping someone would say,oh yeh,I used one from a________ and it fit perfectly.||||reg||1
Z||000005||fieroparts.com||04-03-2001||09:09 PM||||Ok! I will... 1992 Mitsubishi 3000GT<BR>I did this back in 1993 looked real nice,<BR>can't remember how I did?<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by hugh:<BR><B>I was hoping someone would say,oh yeah,I used one from a________ and it fit perfectly.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||14
