Z||000007||LZeitgeist||04-04-2001||05:57 PM||||Mount a red strobe in the backside of the scoop.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||lawrence||04-05-2001||12:37 PM||||One of my Sequential Turn Signal customers (Pig! in the Club listing) installed an LED third light from a late model Cougar.  It looks very nice.<P>I would stay away from the garden variety Radio Shack LEDs for a project like this.  For one, they are likely not bright enough.  Also, for this application, you would want to have matched LEDs, or they will appear different.  My guess is that RS gets whatever LEDs they can, from whomever, cheap.  This isn't the kind of thing you want on your car.<P>Good luck,<P>-L<BR> <A HREF="http://members.nccw.net/webe/sts" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nccw.net/webe/sts</A>  - Sequential Turn Signals||||reg||1
Z||000009||Mr.Frosty||04-05-2001||03:49 PM||||I'm thinking of doing this to my GT.Does anybody know where to get a third light like this that will sit low on the decklid?        <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/gallery/Cars/Vanderhoef1-back.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/gallery/Cars/Vanderhoef1-back.jpg</A>   .It probably will have to be glassed in.<P>------------------<BR>88 Formula T-top <BR>85 GT Turbo<p>[This message has been edited by Mr.Frosty (edited 04-05-2001).]||||reg||5
